  "nativeShape": "Rust Metal renders the named mask_tone_v3 node on original pixels into one private 256-row RGBA32F texture. In each of four bands it checks native source/covered result, uses hardware normalized linear sampling into the independent RGBA32F half, verifies real workgroup counts and drains the submitted command before retaining the half.",
  "negativeControl": "The first primary exposure control reported differences in all four components of one 256-row native band (2,433,024 pixels) and its corresponding half, while its actual final display matched. Replacing the shared diagnostic context with an independent stock proof context and explicitly initializing the baseline texture eliminated the difference on both photos. Those two changes were tested together; the raw first and diagnosed reports are archived.",
